1
00:00:01,721 --> 00:00:03,889
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
FELINE FALL

3
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:38,359
- [bells clinking]
- We offer our humble prayers

4
00:01:38,442 --> 00:01:42,947
to the revered
and awe-inspiring <i>brachiosaurus</i> deity.

5
00:01:43,489 --> 00:01:48,744
We herbivores live
with the threat of death every day.

6
00:01:48,869 --> 00:01:52,289
- [drip]
- Endurify us from all calamities

7
00:01:52,373 --> 00:01:55,376
and cleanse us so that
we may find peace in this life.

8
00:01:55,626 --> 00:01:57,628
Hey, why don't we buy a good luck charm?

9
00:01:57,711 --> 00:02:00,047
Bah! But the talismans are cheaper.

10
00:02:00,131 --> 00:02:02,633
Well, you don't want to
skimp on the offering.

11
00:02:02,716 --> 00:02:05,511
- Come on, it's not like they work.
- [sighs] That's just rude.

12
00:02:05,594 --> 00:02:07,721
- [bells clinking]
- We humbly pray

13
00:02:07,805 --> 00:02:09,890
for protection and prosperity.

14
00:02:10,641 --> 00:02:15,479
Come around, everyone.
Gather 'round. Purify yourselves and pray

15
00:02:15,563 --> 00:02:17,356
that you may avoid being devoured.

16
00:02:18,858 --> 00:02:22,319
[Melon] <i>These types of herbivores
who come to this festival...</i>

17
00:02:22,444 --> 00:02:27,283
<i>fools who casually enjoy
being prey in the food chain.</i>

18
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:31,996
<i>Hmm. But that girl, she is different.</i>

19
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:34,081
That's why I don't understand it.

20
00:02:34,165 --> 00:02:37,960
I've lived every day thinking
it might be the last day that I'm alive.

21
00:02:38,544 --> 00:02:41,922
[Melon] Well, if that's true,
why bother with trying to get a degree,

22
00:02:42,006 --> 00:02:43,674
if you think you're going to die anyway?

23
00:02:44,049 --> 00:02:45,426
[laughs] Come on.

24
00:02:45,509 --> 00:02:47,678
It's not as bleak
as you're making it sound.

25
00:02:47,761 --> 00:02:49,638
It's like, even if I think I might die,

26
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:52,266
there are still some things
I hope I might achieve.

27
00:02:52,349 --> 00:02:53,851
I still have goals and dreams.

28
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,145
[Melon] <i>I do wonder.</i>

29
00:02:56,896 --> 00:03:00,774
<i>Could I taste those thoughts and emotions?</i>

30
00:03:00,858 --> 00:03:03,569
<i>Are they in her blood and flesh?</i>

31
00:03:04,904 --> 00:03:06,822
[Legoshi] Professor Lumrong.

32
00:03:07,072 --> 00:03:08,490
<i>Hmm?</i>

33
00:03:08,824 --> 00:03:11,076
How about... Melon?

34
00:03:12,119 --> 00:03:13,746
I owe you for my ear.

35
00:03:13,829 --> 00:03:16,290
And definitely
when you got me in the stomach,

36
00:03:16,707 --> 00:03:18,459
Is this a ghost?

37
00:03:19,168 --> 00:03:20,711
[chuckles]

38
00:03:20,794 --> 00:03:23,088
You're actually still alive?

39
00:03:23,172 --> 00:03:25,090
Feel like getting killed again?

40
00:03:26,175 --> 00:03:30,221
Sorry to disappoint,
but tonight's not great for me.

41
00:03:30,304 --> 00:03:32,514
Let's try another day, shall we?

42
00:03:32,598 --> 00:03:35,559
- She's not gonna show up.
- Huh?

43
00:03:35,643 --> 00:03:37,978
- Haru, I mean.
- Haru?

44
00:03:39,021 --> 00:03:40,397
You know her?

45
00:03:40,481 --> 00:03:42,650
{\an8}Tonight, you're going down,
no matter what!

46
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:45,402
{\an8}Oh, really?

47
00:03:46,445 --> 00:03:48,489
[loud stomping]

48
00:03:49,114 --> 00:03:52,993
[Haru sighs] Come on.
This is blatant kidnapping. [strains]

49
00:03:53,202 --> 00:03:54,828
[grunts]

50
00:03:54,912 --> 00:03:56,747
[strains] Ah!

51
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,874
Still waiting for an explanation!

52
00:03:58,958 --> 00:04:00,167
- [grunts]
- [stomping]

53
00:04:00,876 --> 00:04:01,919
- [grunts]
- [stomps]

54
00:04:02,795 --> 00:04:05,172
- [stomping]
- Stop it. And quit stomping.

55
00:04:06,382 --> 00:04:08,425
[groans] Are you gonna tell me anything?

56
00:04:08,509 --> 00:04:10,219
I should be at the festival.

57
00:04:10,636 --> 00:04:12,012
Yes, I hear you.

58
00:04:12,096 --> 00:04:13,264
However...

59
00:04:13,889 --> 00:04:16,517
Don't tell me
you're worried about that whole

60
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,769
letting him eat me thing I mentioned.

61
00:04:18,852 --> 00:04:20,938
I told you to mind your own business.

62
00:04:21,021 --> 00:04:22,856
When I meet him
I can just say it was a joke.

63
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,900
You can't joke with a guy like him!

64
00:04:25,192 --> 00:04:29,154
Listen here. The guy you made that
offer to isn't a harmless schoolteacher.

65
00:04:29,238 --> 00:04:31,865
He runs the black market
and he's tried to kill Legoshi

66
00:04:31,949 --> 00:04:33,284
not once, but twice!

67
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:34,410
[gasps]

68
00:04:35,411 --> 00:04:36,495
- [thunder breaks]
- [gasps]

69
00:04:36,578 --> 00:04:38,872
[Melon groans, panting]

70
00:04:38,956 --> 00:04:41,000
[Louis] Please, just stay here today.

71
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:44,169
[groans] Well, give me some food.

72
00:04:44,378 --> 00:04:47,131
[sighs] What do you want?

73
00:04:47,673 --> 00:04:48,924
Veggie sticks.

74
00:04:49,508 --> 00:04:51,885
All right, then. I'll get some.

75
00:04:51,969 --> 00:04:53,304
Don't do anything crazy.

76
00:04:54,096 --> 00:04:55,097
[door opens]

77
00:04:56,307 --> 00:04:57,391
[door closes]

78
00:04:59,643 --> 00:05:01,812
[gasps] Just stop it!

79
00:05:02,187 --> 00:05:03,772
What's your species, Professor?

80
00:05:04,356 --> 00:05:05,649
[Melon] Huh?

81
00:05:05,733 --> 00:05:06,900
Not to worry.

82
00:05:06,984 --> 00:05:08,861
As you can see, I'm a gazelle.

83
00:05:09,028 --> 00:05:13,032
Uh, well, the way you were
holding me wasn't romantic.

84
00:05:13,115 --> 00:05:17,995
It was almost like how a carnivore catches
an herbivore right before they, uh...

85
00:05:18,287 --> 00:05:20,539
Now I see.

86
00:05:20,622 --> 00:05:23,834
So you must be the girl's boyfriend, huh?

87
00:05:23,917 --> 00:05:28,339
[sighs] Guess I won't be
getting my birthday present then, huh?

88
00:05:28,464 --> 00:05:29,798
Why'd you pick Haru?

89
00:05:30,257 --> 00:05:31,842
[scoffing] Why indeed?

90
00:05:31,925 --> 00:05:33,886
[laughs] It should be obvious.

91
00:05:35,637 --> 00:05:37,848
- Same reason as you.
- Huh?

92
00:05:38,557 --> 00:05:41,226
- Because she looks so tasty.
- [gasps]

93
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:43,896
- [Melon laughs]
- [grunts]

94
00:05:43,979 --> 00:05:46,023
Oh, I'm sure you know.

95
00:05:46,106 --> 00:05:48,400
They taste like nothing but sand.

96
00:05:48,484 --> 00:05:49,693
What does?

97
00:05:50,277 --> 00:05:54,031
- Oh. Those who die soaked in fear.
- [sighs]

98
00:05:54,114 --> 00:05:55,949
[Melon laughs]

99
00:05:56,075 --> 00:05:58,660
It literally changes their taste.

100
00:05:59,161 --> 00:06:03,749
Prey tends to fear death
from the very day they're born.

101
00:06:03,832 --> 00:06:05,334
[Legoshi] Everyone's afraid of dying.

102
00:06:05,417 --> 00:06:07,044
- [Melon] Are you sure?
- [inhales sharply]

103
00:06:07,544 --> 00:06:11,340
Remarkably, that little girl of yours...

104
00:06:11,423 --> 00:06:14,259
she's not afraid of dying... or living.

105
00:06:15,177 --> 00:06:18,138
That's why her flesh intrigues me.

106
00:06:18,222 --> 00:06:21,475
[chuckles] You know,
I've grown quite fond of it.

107
00:06:21,558 --> 00:06:22,643
[Melon laughs]

108
00:06:22,726 --> 00:06:24,353
Just like you, I guess.

109
00:06:24,436 --> 00:06:25,354
[Legoshi] No!

110
00:06:26,313 --> 00:06:27,981
{\an8}You don't... It's not like that.

111
00:06:28,065 --> 00:06:29,191
[Melon] Ohh.

112
00:06:29,274 --> 00:06:32,319
Been having a hard time
with those inner urges?

113
00:06:33,112 --> 00:06:34,363
Want some medicine?

114
00:06:34,446 --> 00:06:36,698
- [gun clicks]
- [Legoshi gasps, pants]

115
00:06:37,491 --> 00:06:38,325
[grunts]

116
00:06:38,784 --> 00:06:41,120
- [gunshots]
- [panting]

117
00:06:41,703 --> 00:06:43,247
- [gunshot]
- [exclaims]

118
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:45,833
Today is my birthday, you know.

119
00:06:45,916 --> 00:06:48,001
So in a way, don't you owe me?

120
00:06:48,085 --> 00:06:49,211
Killing me won't do that.

121
00:06:49,294 --> 00:06:51,213
It won't get you any closer to her.

122
00:06:51,296 --> 00:06:53,090
[Melon] Well, here's the thing.

123
00:06:53,841 --> 00:06:55,926
I pretty much do whatever I want.

124
00:06:57,970 --> 00:07:02,724
I will say...
failure and I have met a few times.

125
00:07:04,685 --> 00:07:08,355
I just didn't try hard enough
not to be born.

126
00:07:08,939 --> 00:07:10,858
Huh? "Not to be born"?

127
00:07:10,941 --> 00:07:11,942
[gasps]

128
00:07:12,151 --> 00:07:13,527
[gunshots]

129
00:07:14,695 --> 00:07:16,697
[Melon] My parents were reckless.

130
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:20,033
They fed their flesh
with an interspecies romance,

131
00:07:20,951 --> 00:07:25,247
and as a result, something unnatural
was brought into this world.

132
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:26,748
"Unnatural"?

133
00:07:26,832 --> 00:07:28,917
[Melon] Me, the mistake.

134
00:07:30,335 --> 00:07:33,213
If they'd had any sense,
they wouldn't have brought

135
00:07:33,297 --> 00:07:35,841
a mixed creature into this society.

136
00:07:36,550 --> 00:07:37,551
Don't you agree?

137
00:07:37,634 --> 00:07:41,013
[Legoshi] You're wrong.
Parents deserve our respect, our love.

138
00:07:41,096 --> 00:07:42,890
- And they didn't--
- They didn't think

139
00:07:42,973 --> 00:07:44,516
about anyone but themselves.

140
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:49,062
{\an8}To bring a hybrid child into this world
is just a death sentence.

141
00:07:49,146 --> 00:07:52,733
{\an8}- Huh? It's not a death sentence.
- A painful existence.

142
00:07:54,026 --> 00:07:57,154
Something the parents need to feel.

143
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:02,201
Which is why it falls on me
to exact revenge

144
00:08:02,284 --> 00:08:05,162
for all the mixed children
that haven't been born yet,

145
00:08:05,245 --> 00:08:08,540
before their parents give in
to their selfishness.

146
00:08:08,624 --> 00:08:11,752
[inhales sharply]
Because after they're born, it's too late.

147
00:08:11,919 --> 00:08:14,046
Huh. [gasps]

148
00:08:14,129 --> 00:08:16,256
All of those devourings were you!

149
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:18,300
[Melon laughs] Was it?

150
00:08:18,383 --> 00:08:20,511
- Or maybe it was you.
- What?

151
00:08:20,594 --> 00:08:24,348
Carnivores eat herbivores,
and that's just life.

152
00:08:25,224 --> 00:08:27,100
But this was an experiment.

153
00:08:27,559 --> 00:08:30,312
What links interspecies relationships?

154
00:08:30,395 --> 00:08:32,272
Raw, natural hunger?

155
00:08:33,148 --> 00:08:34,775
Or was it indeed love?

156
00:08:35,317 --> 00:08:36,527
So it was you.

157
00:08:37,319 --> 00:08:38,987
You were the one behind it all.

158
00:08:39,071 --> 00:08:40,948
- [gun cocks]
- [Melon laughs]

159
00:08:42,407 --> 00:08:46,078
Their blood covered expressions
were frozen in bliss.

160
00:08:46,161 --> 00:08:47,371
Damn you. [growls]

161
00:08:47,454 --> 00:08:48,455
You're a monster.

162
00:08:48,539 --> 00:08:49,790
Watch your mouth.

163
00:08:49,873 --> 00:08:51,041
I do what I want.

164
00:08:51,124 --> 00:08:52,125
No!

165
00:08:52,668 --> 00:08:56,463
We live in a society.
We can't just do whatever we want.

166
00:08:56,547 --> 00:08:59,383
Not with dangerous beasts
like you roaming around.

167
00:08:59,466 --> 00:09:01,510
- I'm not like you.
- [laughs]

168
00:09:01,593 --> 00:09:03,220
Everyone says that.

169
00:09:04,388 --> 00:09:06,557
[sighs] In that case...

170
00:09:07,432 --> 00:09:09,268
answer this question for me.

171
00:09:10,018 --> 00:09:11,770
You have two options.

172
00:09:13,063 --> 00:09:18,944
"A". A society without devouring,
but with government surveillance.

173
00:09:20,821 --> 00:09:26,493
"B". A society with devouring,
but zero surveillance.

174
00:09:26,577 --> 00:09:27,661
Which one?

175
00:09:28,745 --> 00:09:30,455
Which would you choose?

176
00:09:30,831 --> 00:09:31,873
Huh?

177
00:09:32,457 --> 00:09:33,959
[Legoshi] <i>I guess, uh...</i>

178
00:09:34,835 --> 00:09:38,088
<i>I'll go with "A".
A society with no devouring.</i>

179
00:09:38,171 --> 00:09:40,257
[Melon] <i>You're okay with being watched?</i>

180
00:09:40,591 --> 00:09:42,759
[Legoshi]
<i>If it keeps everybody safe, it's worth it.</i>

181
00:09:42,843 --> 00:09:45,429
- [Louis] Naru. [sighs]
- [Melon laughs]

182
00:09:45,512 --> 00:09:47,139
[Louis] I told her not to go anywhere.

183
00:09:47,222 --> 00:09:53,437
[Melon] <i>This so called coexistence
and co-prosperity society is a prison</i>

184
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,106
<i>where we're all spying on each other.</i>

185
00:09:56,982 --> 00:09:58,609
{\an8}Where the hell are you?

186
00:10:01,278 --> 00:10:04,281
Wearing restraint like a straitjacket.

187
00:10:04,364 --> 00:10:05,907
Living, but not free.

188
00:10:05,991 --> 00:10:07,492
That's a prisoner.

189
00:10:07,993 --> 00:10:10,078
That's what you all are.

190
00:10:10,329 --> 00:10:13,790
[inhales sharply] But me...
I'm not like you.

191
00:10:14,541 --> 00:10:16,585
I choose "B".

192
00:10:16,668 --> 00:10:20,839
Devouring is thrilling,
delicious, pure vitality.

193
00:10:20,922 --> 00:10:23,467
Gushing with so many colors of life.

194
00:10:23,550 --> 00:10:24,843
You get it, right?

195
00:10:25,886 --> 00:10:27,846
If you're a carnivore, that is.

196
00:10:28,347 --> 00:10:29,723
[sighs]

197
00:10:29,806 --> 00:10:32,142
[Legoshi]
<i>That's what's caused me so much pain.</i>

198
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:36,438
[Melon] Why would you
suppress your true self?

199
00:10:36,521 --> 00:10:39,232
Following the rules? Being a good boy?

200
00:10:39,316 --> 00:10:41,193
[Melon scoffs, laughs]

201
00:10:41,276 --> 00:10:43,570
That sounds like living to you?

202
00:10:43,654 --> 00:10:46,031
[Legoshi] It is, if it means
that no one has to die.

203
00:10:46,114 --> 00:10:49,368
So I guess the less suffering,
the happier you are.

204
00:10:49,743 --> 00:10:52,079
[inhales sharply] I see.

205
00:10:52,704 --> 00:10:55,123
So it sounds like your solution is

206
00:10:55,207 --> 00:10:57,668
"if it doesn't fit, wipe it out."

207
00:10:59,252 --> 00:11:03,632
Ah. It's been a while
since I thought about their voices.

208
00:11:04,591 --> 00:11:10,555
The good boys who tried to wipe me out
just because I existed.

209
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:14,309
- [kid 1] <i>Jump, jump, jump!
-</i> [kid 2] <i>Jump!</i>

210
00:11:14,393 --> 00:11:15,394
- Do it already!
- Come on!

211
00:11:15,477 --> 00:11:17,145
Why don't you be a good little herbivore?

212
00:11:17,229 --> 00:11:19,398
Why don't you land
on those big sharp fangs?

213
00:11:19,481 --> 00:11:21,024
Don't cats always land on their feet?

214
00:11:21,108 --> 00:11:23,360
If you take after your mom,
you probably won't die.

215
00:11:23,443 --> 00:11:26,154
If you don't make it, you won't
have to go to school tomorrow.

216
00:11:26,238 --> 00:11:28,657
- Jump already! Do everyone a favor.
- Just jump, you coward!

217
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:30,117
- Come on, just do it!
- Jump! Jump!

218
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,451
- Jump!
- [kids laugh]

219
00:11:31,535 --> 00:11:34,246
- [shouts]
- [scream echoes]

220
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:38,792
[Melon] <i>I was nine,
and I killed my classmates.</i>

221
00:11:39,668 --> 00:11:42,337
<i>But that was the first time I felt free.</i>

222
00:11:43,296 --> 00:11:44,506
But, you know...

223
00:11:45,298 --> 00:11:48,009
I do wonder if I had jumped back then...

224
00:11:48,093 --> 00:11:51,221
do you think I would have
grown a pair of wings?

225
00:11:51,304 --> 00:11:54,307
Then I would have been
free to fly wherever I wanted.

226
00:11:55,058 --> 00:11:58,145
Huh. What a perfect thought.

227
00:11:58,770 --> 00:12:01,022
Anyway, keep your eye on the prize.

228
00:12:01,106 --> 00:12:02,482
- [Melon chuckles]
- Huh?

229
00:12:02,566 --> 00:12:04,776
No, no. No, no!

230
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:07,988
No!

231
00:12:08,738 --> 00:12:11,324
[thrilling music playing]

232
00:12:14,161 --> 00:12:15,078
[both grunting]

233
00:12:16,496 --> 00:12:18,165
[Legoshi] <i>You're not gonna get away.</i>

234
00:12:18,915 --> 00:12:20,208
[both groaning]

235
00:12:22,794 --> 00:12:23,837
[groaning]

236
00:12:25,547 --> 00:12:26,673
[Melon groans]

237
00:12:26,756 --> 00:12:29,050
- Come on! Let's go!
- Huh?

238
00:12:29,509 --> 00:12:30,677
[Legoshi] Move it!

239
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,638
- [Melon] What? Where to?
- A police station.

240
00:12:34,514 --> 00:12:36,641
Listen, please don't make me carry you.

241
00:12:37,267 --> 00:12:39,311
[Melon grunting]

242
00:12:41,021 --> 00:12:43,815
[laughs scornfully] The police, huh?

243
00:12:43,899 --> 00:12:47,277
Well, maybe jail
wouldn't be so bad for me.

244
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:50,030
<i>But if I'm in jail, does that mean</i>

245
00:12:50,113 --> 00:12:52,532
<i>I'll miss out on eating
that lovely rabbit?</i>

246
00:12:53,158 --> 00:12:54,534
[Legoshi] <i>He's going to the cops,</i>

247
00:12:54,618 --> 00:12:57,329
<i>and then I'll have Yahya
take care of my record,</i>

248
00:12:57,412 --> 00:12:58,747
<i>so I can marry Haru.</i>

249
00:12:58,830 --> 00:13:01,625
[Melon] <i>If I don't eat that rabbit,
I'll be filled with regret...</i>

250
00:13:02,542 --> 00:13:04,419
<i>never knowing what delicious really means.</i>

251
00:13:04,503 --> 00:13:06,171
[Legoshi] <i>Then we'll be together forever.</i>

252
00:13:06,254 --> 00:13:09,007
- [Melon] <i>Just one bite would be enough.</i>
- [Legoshi] <i>Me and Haru.</i>

253
00:13:11,009 --> 00:13:12,594
[both stammer]

254
00:13:14,387 --> 00:13:17,349
Well, now I see how strong
a carnivore can be.

255
00:13:17,432 --> 00:13:19,643
- Huh?
- You've got quite a grip.

256
00:13:19,726 --> 00:13:20,977
It's like iron.

257
00:13:21,811 --> 00:13:24,397
Pull much harder
and you're gonna break my arm.

258
00:13:24,481 --> 00:13:26,483
I'm sure as a wolf cub
that you were taught

259
00:13:26,566 --> 00:13:29,319
to take it easy on those weaker than you.

260
00:13:30,445 --> 00:13:31,446
Uh...

261
00:13:31,530 --> 00:13:32,531
[Legoshi] <i>He's right.</i>

262
00:13:32,614 --> 00:13:34,282
<i>This rage running through me...</i>

263
00:13:34,366 --> 00:13:35,492
<i>I can feel it.</i>

264
00:13:35,742 --> 00:13:37,494
[Melon grunts]

265
00:13:37,577 --> 00:13:38,620
[Legoshi] Hey!

266
00:13:41,373 --> 00:13:42,958
[Melon laughs maniacally]

267
00:13:43,041 --> 00:13:46,628
If I had my way,
I'd gut you with my horns.

268
00:13:46,711 --> 00:13:49,422
- [Legoshi grunts]
- Ooh! [laughs]

269
00:13:50,006 --> 00:13:52,300
I think you've gotten quicker.

270
00:13:52,384 --> 00:13:55,095
Still only slightly faster
than a sloth, though.

271
00:13:55,178 --> 00:13:57,389
- [Legoshi] This isn't a joke!
- Ooh!

272
00:13:57,764 --> 00:13:59,683
[Legoshi grunting]

273
00:14:02,561 --> 00:14:04,396
[Melon] Whoo! [laughs]

274
00:14:04,563 --> 00:14:06,064
Yeah! [laughs mischievously]

275
00:14:06,147 --> 00:14:07,315
Gah!

276
00:14:08,191 --> 00:14:09,609
Help me!

277
00:14:10,569 --> 00:14:11,570
Help me!

278
00:14:11,653 --> 00:14:13,280
This wolf is going to eat me!

279
00:14:13,363 --> 00:14:15,031
[panting] There he is!

280
00:14:15,115 --> 00:14:17,242
- [guard 1] Who's that?
- [guard 2] Go. We got this.

281
00:14:17,325 --> 00:14:18,785
Carnivores aren't allowed here.

282
00:14:18,869 --> 00:14:20,370
That guy is a devourer.

283
00:14:20,453 --> 00:14:21,454
He's getting away!

284
00:14:21,538 --> 00:14:24,457
- [guard 1] This guy's crazy.
- [guard 2] Listen, buddy, calm down.

285
00:14:24,541 --> 00:14:26,877
[groans, yells] Melon!

286
00:14:31,756 --> 00:14:33,675
- [bushes rustling]
- Haru, is that you?

287
00:14:35,927 --> 00:14:37,637
[gasping]

288
00:14:37,721 --> 00:14:38,930
What are you doing?

289
00:14:39,014 --> 00:14:41,349
I... I think I dropped my ring out here.

290
00:14:41,433 --> 00:14:43,685
Why wouldn't you bring
a flashlight out here with you?

291
00:14:43,768 --> 00:14:46,646
- Well, I...
- [cell phone buzzes]

292
00:14:46,730 --> 00:14:48,565
[Legoshi] <i>Hey, Louis, it's me.</i>

293
00:14:48,648 --> 00:14:49,649
You got Melon?

294
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:51,401
<i>I lost him.</i>

295
00:14:51,902 --> 00:14:53,695
{\an8}Yeah, same thing here.

296
00:14:53,778 --> 00:14:55,697
{\an8}<i>-What?</i>
- It seems like Haru ran off

297
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,324
{\an8}- while I wasn't looking.
<i>- What?</i>

298
00:14:58,199 --> 00:14:59,701
She might be headed your way.

299
00:14:59,784 --> 00:15:02,245
<i>- All right, got it.</i>
- Call me back, okay?

300
00:15:03,413 --> 00:15:04,623
[sighs]

301
00:15:04,706 --> 00:15:05,707
Just great.

302
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:08,293
Are you... Are you looking for Haru?

303
00:15:08,376 --> 00:15:09,419
Huh?

304
00:15:10,545 --> 00:15:13,465
[Haru] Hmm.
So if you want to open a restaurant,

305
00:15:13,548 --> 00:15:16,134
you have to think about
more than just the food, right?

306
00:15:16,217 --> 00:15:18,845
Well, that's definitely something
you want to consider.

307
00:15:18,929 --> 00:15:21,056
Haru! So what happened to staying put?

308
00:15:21,139 --> 00:15:22,849
- Yeah, sorry about that.
- [panting]

309
00:15:22,933 --> 00:15:25,936
I went to the bathroom
and this big bookshelf caught my eye.

310
00:15:26,019 --> 00:15:28,063
She mentioned that she wants
to open a restaurant,

311
00:15:28,146 --> 00:15:30,774
so I merely suggested
she study management as well.

312
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:32,275
- [Haru laughs]
- [Louis sighs]

313
00:15:32,776 --> 00:15:34,027
Not bad advice.

314
00:15:34,945 --> 00:15:36,404
Well, you found me.

315
00:15:36,488 --> 00:15:38,573
Listen, even I know
when it's time to behave.

316
00:15:38,657 --> 00:15:41,201
- And leaving her room is how you behave?
- I already said sorry.

317
00:15:41,284 --> 00:15:44,245
- One more. It's a good one, too.
- Oh. Thank you so much.

318
00:15:44,329 --> 00:15:46,247
What the... [sighs in exasperation]

319
00:15:46,331 --> 00:15:47,540
Seriously!

320
00:15:47,624 --> 00:15:49,417
You are unbelievable.

321
00:15:50,627 --> 00:15:53,254
[Yahya] I already told you
those things don't work.

322
00:15:53,338 --> 00:15:55,548
[Peach] Wait, you didn't
buy the good luck charm.

323
00:15:55,632 --> 00:15:59,386
It's Legoshi. I can't find Melon anywhere.

324
00:15:59,469 --> 00:16:01,805
- Haru isn't here either.
- [Haru] <i>Is that Legoshi?</i>

325
00:16:02,347 --> 00:16:04,224
{\an8}- Haru?
- [Louis] <i>Here she is.</i>

326
00:16:04,641 --> 00:16:07,102
[sighs, stammers] Are you doing okay?

327
00:16:07,185 --> 00:16:09,479
- You're not hurt, are you?
- [Legoshi] <i>No, I... I'm okay.</i>

328
00:16:09,562 --> 00:16:10,814
I was worried.

329
00:16:10,897 --> 00:16:12,649
<i>Don't worry. It's not your fault.</i>

330
00:16:12,983 --> 00:16:14,901
<i>I'm just glad that you're safe.</i>

331
00:16:15,402 --> 00:16:18,571
Louis' father... I have to say,
he's really an interesting guy.

332
00:16:18,655 --> 00:16:22,492
He knows about so many things. [chuckles]
And he looks a bit like Louis.

333
00:16:22,575 --> 00:16:24,077
[Legoshi laughs]

334
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,286
I'd love to meet him.

335
00:16:25,370 --> 00:16:27,497
Before that,
you're the only one I wanna see.

336
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,666
[Haru] <i>Oh. How about tomorrow?</i>

337
00:16:29,749 --> 00:16:32,043
{\an8}All right. I'll come meet you
when you get out of school.

338
00:16:32,127 --> 00:16:34,004
{\an8}<i>Nice.</i> [giggles] <i>See you then.</i>

339
00:16:34,087 --> 00:16:35,630
{\an8}You're so great.

340
00:16:36,464 --> 00:16:38,758
{\an8}- [Louis] <i>That's weird.</i>
- Oh, um... Louis.

341
00:16:38,842 --> 00:16:40,343
{\an8}<i>So what's the plan now?</i>

342
00:16:40,427 --> 00:16:41,636
{\an8}Well, uh...

343
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:46,057
{\an8}So I learned he's the one who's behind
all those recent devourings.

344
00:16:46,141 --> 00:16:47,976
<i>So that was Melon.</i>

345
00:16:48,059 --> 00:16:49,352
<i>Did you go to the police?</i>

346
00:16:49,436 --> 00:16:50,937
I don't have any evidence.

347
00:16:51,021 --> 00:16:52,105
<i>Gotcha.</i>

348
00:16:52,188 --> 00:16:55,233
I really hope we catch him soon.
He's not gonna stop till we do.

349
00:16:55,316 --> 00:16:56,359
<i>Right.</i>

350
00:16:56,443 --> 00:16:58,570
<i>I'll look into it on my end, too.</i>

351
00:16:58,653 --> 00:17:00,238
<i>Just don't do anything crazy.</i>

352
00:17:00,321 --> 00:17:02,407
{\an8}I appreciate you taking care of Haru.

353
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:03,575
<i>Of course.</i>

354
00:17:04,117 --> 00:17:05,326
[Yahya] Hold on.

355
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:06,578
[Peach] What's this?

356
00:17:06,661 --> 00:17:09,122
So you did buy one, you goofball.

357
00:17:09,330 --> 00:17:10,540
Aw!

358
00:17:15,462 --> 00:17:17,297
[cicadas chirping]

359
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,423
[Free grunting]

360
00:17:19,924 --> 00:17:22,385
[grunting]

361
00:17:22,719 --> 00:17:24,512
[sighs] Here you go.

362
00:17:25,055 --> 00:17:27,307
All right. You guys know
how this whole thing works.

363
00:17:27,390 --> 00:17:31,394
The whiskers will tell us if this year's
turf war is something we're gonna do.

364
00:17:31,478 --> 00:17:33,521
If the whiskers move to the right,

365
00:17:33,605 --> 00:17:36,441
then we'll pick a representative
and send them out.

366
00:17:36,524 --> 00:17:38,526
But if they end up moving to the left.

367
00:17:38,610 --> 00:17:39,819
[cell phone ringing]

368
00:17:40,487 --> 00:17:42,280
Sorry. Hang on a sec.

369
00:17:43,239 --> 00:17:44,866
- Hey, Louis!
- Oh!

370
00:17:45,492 --> 00:17:48,536
Change your mind
about being our boss again?

371
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,288
What? Melon?

372
00:17:50,371 --> 00:17:52,123
Do you know where he is?

373
00:17:52,207 --> 00:17:55,085
[Free] <i>He hasn't shown his face
around here lately.</i>

374
00:17:55,168 --> 00:17:57,629
<i>And I know he hasn't been
around the black market.</i>

375
00:17:58,338 --> 00:17:59,422
I see.

376
00:17:59,964 --> 00:18:01,049
Thanks for your help.

377
00:18:01,132 --> 00:18:03,259
If you hear anything about him,
please let me know.

378
00:18:03,343 --> 00:18:06,221
[sighs] <i>You know I would if I could.</i>

379
00:18:06,304 --> 00:18:08,014
<i>He's still the boss after all.</i>

380
00:18:08,098 --> 00:18:10,642
He's a devouring maniac
with no honor whatsoever,

381
00:18:10,725 --> 00:18:12,143
but he's still your boss, huh?

382
00:18:12,227 --> 00:18:13,770
<i>I don't make the rules.</i>

383
00:18:14,687 --> 00:18:16,523
Well, I'm counting on you anyway.

384
00:18:20,527 --> 00:18:21,611
MELON

385
00:18:22,112 --> 00:18:24,781
[Louis] <i>So he hasn't been
around the black market.</i>

386
00:18:24,864 --> 00:18:26,074
<i>What do I do?</i>

387
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:29,119
<i>Should I go on television
and warn people about him?</i>

388
00:18:29,577 --> 00:18:31,246
[sighs] <i>No, I can't.</i>

389
00:18:31,329 --> 00:18:32,831
<i>Not without evidence.</i>

390
00:18:32,914 --> 00:18:34,582
<i>It'll just cause a panic.</i>

391
00:18:35,416 --> 00:18:37,627
<i>Should I tell Yahya what's going on?</i>

392
00:18:38,002 --> 00:18:40,547
<i>No. He probably knows already.</i>

393
00:18:40,630 --> 00:18:42,090
- [door opens]
<i>- Hmm?</i>

394
00:18:42,507 --> 00:18:43,842
Hey there, Louis.

395
00:18:43,925 --> 00:18:46,344
Some tough opponents
will be out there today.

396
00:18:46,427 --> 00:18:48,638
You don't have to speak
if you don't want to.

397
00:18:48,721 --> 00:18:51,724
There's no need to risk going out
and saying the wrong thing.

398
00:18:51,808 --> 00:18:55,687
Listen, just having you on the screen
for a moment is enough of a win for us.

399
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:57,021
[laughs]

400
00:18:57,105 --> 00:18:58,398
[Louis sighs]

401
00:18:59,691 --> 00:19:01,484
{\an8}MELON

402
00:19:01,776 --> 00:19:04,696
{\an8}Does it smell like
cheap coffee in here to you?

403
00:19:04,779 --> 00:19:05,780
{\an8}Let's fix that.

404
00:19:05,864 --> 00:19:09,284
{\an8}We can't have our ambassador drinking
that cheap instant dishwater.

405
00:19:09,617 --> 00:19:12,745
Oh, actually have you ever tried
drinking Kopi luwak?

406
00:19:12,829 --> 00:19:14,330
It's really tasty.

407
00:19:14,414 --> 00:19:16,291
Next time I see you, it's on me.

408
00:19:16,374 --> 00:19:18,293
All right. It's showtime.

409
00:19:18,376 --> 00:19:19,878
Smiles, big smiles!

410
00:19:20,879 --> 00:19:22,088
[door closes]

411
00:19:22,797 --> 00:19:24,257
Kopi luwak?

412
00:19:24,883 --> 00:19:26,301
UDON BEBEBE

413
00:19:26,384 --> 00:19:28,386
[Sunaga] Heads up. You have a delivery.

414
00:19:29,512 --> 00:19:30,972
[Sheila] Okay.

415
00:19:31,055 --> 00:19:32,891
It's in the First Ocean District.

416
00:19:33,391 --> 00:19:35,435
You don't happen to speak
a little Ocean language?

417
00:19:35,518 --> 00:19:38,146
[speaking Ocean language]

418
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:41,274
Wow! Very impressive!

419
00:19:41,357 --> 00:19:44,068
I didn't graduate
from Cherryton School for nothing.

420
00:19:44,402 --> 00:19:46,070
Well, that's wonderful.

421
00:19:46,362 --> 00:19:49,866
I bet you could do more around here
than just filling in for Legoshi.

422
00:19:50,742 --> 00:19:52,368
And speaking of Legoshi,

423
00:19:52,452 --> 00:19:54,746
he didn't tell me
he was taking any time off.

424
00:19:54,829 --> 00:19:55,914
Have you heard anything?

425
00:19:55,997 --> 00:19:57,248
{\an8}No, I haven't.

426
00:19:57,332 --> 00:19:59,792
{\an8}He must have a good reason
for not being here, though.

427
00:19:59,876 --> 00:20:01,544
{\an8}He's kind of awkward with his words.

428
00:20:01,628 --> 00:20:03,546
{\an8}So most of the time he gets misunderstood.

429
00:20:03,630 --> 00:20:05,882
Was that how he was at school as well?

430
00:20:05,965 --> 00:20:07,884
He mumbled something once.

431
00:20:07,967 --> 00:20:11,054
Said the udon here is delicious
and the boss is handsome.

432
00:20:11,137 --> 00:20:12,472
All right, I'm off.

433
00:20:13,806 --> 00:20:16,559
You know, he really is such a good kid.

434
00:20:17,977 --> 00:20:19,604
[Legoshi] Hmm.

435
00:20:20,230 --> 00:20:21,231
Hmm.

436
00:20:21,314 --> 00:20:23,024
Hmm. [sighs]

437
00:20:24,776 --> 00:20:28,613
Louis told me about the Shishi-Gumi
technique for making decisions.

438
00:20:28,905 --> 00:20:31,032
I don't know if wolf whiskers work.

439
00:20:32,283 --> 00:20:33,660
Melon...

440
00:20:33,743 --> 00:20:35,578
He said he quit the university.

441
00:20:36,496 --> 00:20:39,290
I just need a little hint
about where he might be.

442
00:20:39,791 --> 00:20:41,918
- [wind blows]
- Hmm. Hold on.

443
00:20:45,213 --> 00:20:46,756
The tattoo studio?

444
00:20:47,090 --> 00:20:49,008
[Melon laughs]

445
00:20:49,092 --> 00:20:51,511
I think you've gotten quicker.

446
00:20:51,594 --> 00:20:54,430
Still only slightly faster
than a sloth, though.

447
00:20:54,722 --> 00:20:55,890
There's no way!

448
00:20:57,016 --> 00:21:00,186
{\an8}THE BLUE DRAGON

449
00:21:02,146 --> 00:21:03,856
Can I come in?

450
00:21:04,691 --> 00:21:05,775
Uh...

451
00:21:08,403 --> 00:21:09,487
Hmm.

452
00:21:10,238 --> 00:21:11,239
[gasps]

453
00:21:14,409 --> 00:21:15,410
Uh, hey, man.

454
00:21:17,912 --> 00:21:19,414
Uh... [shudders] Oh, no!

455
00:21:20,248 --> 00:21:21,833
[panicked] Uh, anyone here?

456
00:21:21,916 --> 00:21:23,001
[gasps]

457
00:21:25,586 --> 00:21:26,921
[siren wailing in distance]

458
00:21:27,005 --> 00:21:28,506
Uh... Oh, crap.

459
00:21:28,881 --> 00:21:30,508
I definitely shouldn't be here.

460
00:21:30,591 --> 00:21:32,802
- [siren continues]
- [panting] I'm sorry.

461
00:21:33,094 --> 00:21:34,554
[tires screech]

462
00:21:40,018 --> 00:21:41,144
[grunts softly]

463
00:21:43,354 --> 00:21:45,565
Hey! I got eyes on a wolf!

464
00:21:45,648 --> 00:21:46,941
Hold it right there!

465
00:21:47,025 --> 00:21:48,026
Hey, stop!

466
00:21:49,110 --> 00:21:50,987
[cop] We've got two victims on site.

467
00:21:51,321 --> 00:21:52,238
Yes.

468
00:21:53,531 --> 00:21:56,492
Confirming, both are deceased. Hmm.

469
00:21:56,576 --> 00:21:58,119
Go ahead and send Forensics.

470
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:03,082
[closing theme song playing]
